{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase_zD_im_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase_zD_im_odd","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L195-L199","doc":"The `D`-frame rung phase has `Im` odd in `ε`. Concrete corollary; the\ngeneral statement above is the one that carries the immunity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.zD_reflective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.zD_reflective","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L186-L193","doc":"`z_D` is reflective — it is a rational function with rational\ncoefficients. Together with `alphaPhase_im_odd_of_reflective_markov` this\ndischarges the `D`-frame half of the immunity claim in Lean; the `C`-frame\nhalf needs the principal branch of `√q` (outside this file's algebraic\nscope) and is measured instead, at 60 dps, by probe assertion A8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.zD","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L182-L184","doc":"Convention **D** (SU(2)/Temperley–Lieb Jones; owner ruling 2026-08-09):\n`z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase_im_odd_of_reflective_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase_im_odd_of_reflective_markov","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L174-L180","doc":"**The parity, for any convention.** `Im α(q₀ − iε) = − Im α(q₀ + iε)`\nwhenever the Markov parameter is reflective — the `C`/`D`/anything\nstatement the KC21 immunity claim needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase_reflective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase_reflective","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L161-L172","doc":"**The convention-immunity statement.** For *every* reflective Markov\nparameter, the rung phase is reflective.\n\nThis quantifies over conventions: it is not a fact about `z_C`, nor about\n`z_D`, but about the whole class. A future convention change cannot break\nit unless the new `z` is non-reflective — i.e. unless it fails to be\nreal-valued on the real `q`-axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.alphaPhase","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L153-L159","doc":"The `N=1` rung phase `α = (z−1)·h/2` with `h = q − q⁻¹`, as a function of\nthe substrate parameter, **parameterised by the Markov parameter `z`**.\nThis is the site where the trace convention enters the `Q_β` ladder\n(`qbeta_utils.py:124-125`; the same `z` in the exact-series core at\n`qbeta_ck_sseries_exact_rational.py:20,248`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.comp","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L143-L147","doc":"Reflectivity is closed under composition — so a ladder built by\nsubstituting one reflective expression into another stays reflective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.pow","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L139-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.div","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L135-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.inv","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L130-L133","doc":"Reflectivity survives inversion — `ℂ` is a field and `starRingEnd` is a\nring hom, so `conj (x⁻¹) = (conj x)⁻¹` including at `x = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.neg","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L127-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.mul","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L123-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.sub","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L119-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective.add","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L115-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_id","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L111-L113","doc":"The identity is reflective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_const_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_const_real","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L107-L109","doc":"A real constant is reflective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_im_real_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_im_real_zero","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L93-L99","doc":"**Real substrate carries no decay projection.** At `ε = 0` the imaginary\npart vanishes — the generalisation of `fig8Trace_im_real_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_re_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_re_even","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L83-L91","doc":"**Reflective ⇒ `Re` is even in `ε`.** The companion of `reflective_im_odd`,\nand the reason the *literal* reading of KC21's `S(−ε) = −S(ε)` is false:\nthe real part is even and generically nonzero, so the full value is not an\nodd function of `ε`. Only the imaginary part / decay projection is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_im_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.reflective_im_odd","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L72-L81","doc":"**Reflective ⇒ `Im` is odd in `ε`.** `Im f(q₀ − iε) = − Im f(q₀ + iε)`.\n\nThis is the generalisation of `fig8Trace_im_odd`: the hypothesis is a\nproperty of `f`, not of its construction, so no ingredient of `f` — the\nMarkov parameter included — appears in the statement or the proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderParityReflection.Reflective","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderParityReflection.lean#L60-L66","doc":"A map is **reflective** when complex conjugation commutes with it:\n`f(conj z) = conj (f z)`. Every function built from real constants by the\nfield operations and composition is reflective (see the closure lemmas\nbelow); `fig8TraceC_conj` is the concrete instance for the figure-eight\ntrace. ","signatureChunk":0}]}